# Deny-by-default. This repo versions OPERATING DOCTRINE only.
#
# Everything under .claude/ is ignored unless explicitly un-ignored below, so a
# new file can NEVER be committed by accident. Notably excluded and intended to
# stay that way:
#   projects/    session transcripts (huge) AND seat memory (private)
#   worktrees/   git worktrees of ANOTHER repo — never nest them here
#   settings*    may hold tokens; never version credentials
#   agent-memory/, *.bak, *.lock
#
# To version something new, un-ignore it EXPLICITLY and re-run the secret scan.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/skills/
!/agents/
!/hooks/
!/commands/
!/README.md

# ── The hole an allow-list leaves, closed structurally ────────────────────────
# Un-ignoring a DIRECTORY re-admits everything nested inside it, including
# categories denied above. Found 2026-07-29: `agents/.claude/agent-memory/`
# (4 files, incl. a user-profile) was swallowed by `!/agents/` even though seat
# memory is excluded as a category one level up. Benign that time. Deny the
# CATEGORY at any depth so the next one cannot ride in on the same hole.
**/agent-memory/
**/.claude/
**/memory/
**/*.bak
**/*.lock
